        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI am currently (on and off) looking for an automated solution for typo detection in CI and local fixes. This is mostly to not have a ton of `docs: fix typo` commits, which pollutes the changelog during plugin updates.\r\n\r\nSo in the meantime I'd only have changes that fix factually incorrect documentation (like \"Jump to word start\" instead of intended \"Jump to line start\"). Preferably as a single `docs(jump2d): improve documentation` commit if there are several such changes.",
