        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> * line 22: Corrects indentation.\r\n\r\nCurrent formatting is correct as the example is for `Allowed lines:` and not overall customization.\r\n\r\n> * line 360: I don't understand `(follow by typing one character)`.\r\n\r\nIt describes that after executing the call user should type one character.\r\n\r\n> * line 561: Somehow, this single line always auto formats to 3 lines.\r\n\r\nIt does not. Probably you have StyLua version newer than 0.19.0 (which is [what is used for formatting](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#formatting)). I've looked and there is now a stable version 2.1.0, so will have to change to use it in all modules.\r\n\r\n> * line 79: The spotter in example is `line`, not `word`.\r\n> \r\n> * line 343: Renders like `local values.config|` in help.\r\n\r\nThose are indeed not intended. Please, include only them in a single commit together with typos already present in this PR.",
